While the one-shot approaches rely on a rule-based decoding process to generate the ﬁnal prediction, the attention-based models are closer to the human way of reading: they learn the reading order. However, contrary to one-shot approaches, the recurrence is inherent to the attention-based models, theoretically leading to higher prediction times, especially with character-level attention. It led us to think that both approaches should be investigated.

